	'k80a28809' => 'Seven people',
	'k81049792' => 'Ibuki Cardiology is conveniently located in central Northbridge with lift access from the main entrance lobby. Contact our reception team or visit our follow-up desk during clinic hours.',
	'k811289b7' => 'Every initial assessment is allotted ninety unhurried minutes, timed to the quarter hour. From your arrival at reception through nursing triage, resting ECG, transthoracic echocardiogram, and direct physician consultation, each step proceeds without delay. You leave with an established clinical plan and scheduled next steps. Please bring your photo ID, current medication list, and any prior ECGs or referral letters.',
	'k8276b66d' => 'The ninety-minute schedule',
	'k827b0cdd' => 'New patients can arrange an initial consultation by calling our front desk at +1 555 0142 between 08:00 and 17:30 or by sending an online request. Our patient coordinator Amara Diallo will confirm an appointment slot and provide guidance on what documentation to bring. Physician referrals are welcomed but not mandatory. Initial visits are scheduled during weekday clinic sessions, with fee options including the $180 first consultation or the $420 comprehensive heart check.',
	'k83f14533' => '90 minutes',
	'k85561067' => 'Ibuki Cardiology issues operational notes and clinical education articles throughout the working month. Written by our cardiologists, cardiac nurse Jonas Berg, and sonographer Priya Natarajan, these articles provide practical instructions on preparing for tests, recording home blood pressure accurately, and understanding cardiovascular risk factors. Schedule adjustments, holiday closures, and clinic news are posted promptly to keep Northbridge patients informed of changes before their appointments.',
	'k869e90e1' => 'High readings at school; 24-hour monitor on a Tuesday, a plan with Dr. Ribeiro.',
	'k8741b812' => '“I wanted a clinic where the time on the appointment card is the time you are seen, and where the call about your results comes from someone who knows your name.”',
	'k87e181ac' => 'For established patients who find weekday appointments challenging due to work or family commitments, Ibuki Cardiology operates a Saturday morning clinic from 09:00 to 12:30. This Saturday session is reserved strictly for follow-up consultations, blood pressure reviews, and routine treatment assessments. New patient evaluations and initial diagnostic procedures are not scheduled on Saturdays to preserve dedicated, unhurried time for ongoing review. Weekday consult hours run 08:30 to 17:00, while Sunday and public holidays remain closed.',
