	'ka7d5b386' => 'Ongoing cardiovascular care requires consistent observation, scheduled testing, and clear communication between visits. Ibuki Cardiology provides reliable follow-up consultations tailored to each patient\'s stability and clinical needs.',
	'ka8443b82' => 'Your initial appointment follows a structured sequence designed to avoid unnecessary delays. For an 08:30 arrival, check-in takes ten minutes at reception, followed by fifteen minutes with our cardiac nurse for vital signs, resting blood pressure, and a twelve-lead electrocardiogram. At 08:55, chief cardiac sonographer Priya Natarajan conducts a thirty-minute transthoracic echocardiogram. At 09:25, you spend twenty-five minutes with your cardiologist reviewing ultrasound images and clinical history. The final ten minutes, concluding at 10:00, are dedicated to agreeing on a treatment plan and scheduling follow-up reviews.',
	'ka8fa3895' => 'All published guides regarding continuous Holter monitoring, ambulatory blood pressure logs, and exercise recovery are freely accessible on our website. Patients preparing for a Thursday imaging appointment or Friday prevention visit can review testing requirements in advance. While these articles provide informative context on diagnostic investigations and clinic operations, they do not replace direct clinical consultation. Individual medical questions should be addressed during scheduled appointments or with our follow-up desk.',
	'kaa19b528' => 'Independent outpatient cardiology',
	'kaa87d3ca' => 'Fridays conclude the clinic week with cardiovascular prevention, risk stratification, and return-to-activity assessments directed by Dr. Tomás Ribeiro. This service supports adults with a strong family history of heart disease, elevated cholesterol, or individuals seeking structured guidance before resuming vigorous exercise and competitive sport. Consultations evaluate lifestyle factors, lipid profiles, and cardiovascular endurance, translating diagnostic findings into safe exercise boundaries and actionable long-term preventive targets that fit each patient\'s professional and personal life.',
	'kab2cbf4f' => '09:00–12:30, follow-ups only',
	'kab5b5f1d' => 'Our clinic is open Monday through Friday from 08:00 to 17:30. Consultations run between 08:30 and 17:00, with first-visit echo appointments starting from 08:30. On Saturdays, we open from 09:00 to 12:30 for scheduled follow-ups only. The dedicated follow-up desk operates weekdays from 13:00 to 16:00. The clinic is closed on Sundays and public holidays. Telephone enquiries can be directed to +1 555 0142 or sent via email to desk@ibuki-cardiology.example.',
	'kac2364d8' => 'Continuous ambulatory monitoring captures cardiovascular variations during ordinary daily routines. The 24-hour Holter monitor ($160) records electrical activity via lightweight chest leads to capture palpitations, pauses, or atrial fibrillation. The 24-hour blood pressure monitor ($120) inflates a comfortable arm cuff at regular intervals across day and night to identify nocturnal hypertension and therapy response. Both monitors are fitted during weekday mornings, worn throughout standard activities, and returned the next day for physician reporting.',
