	'ke4f145c9' => 'Following any diagnostic test or procedural monitor, our clinical team conducts an internal review within fourteen days and calls you directly to report results. Long-term follow-up consultations are typically arranged at three, six, or twelve-month intervals depending on clinical stability and the recommendation of your cardiologist. Patients managing heart failure or adjusting complex blood pressure therapies often attend every three months, whereas stable preventative patients are seen annually. A twenty-minute follow-up consultation is priced at $95.',
